        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Aristotle\n- Works: Rhetoric\n- Concepts: rhetoric, five canons of rhetoric\n- Places: Stagira, Chalkidice, Classical Greece\n\nFacts:\n- Aristotle was an ancient Greek philosopher and scientist who lived from 384 BC to 322 BC.\n- Aristotle was born in the city of Stagira in Chalkidice on the northern periphery of Classical Greece.\n- Aristotle wrote the philosophical work \"Rhetoric,\" which still has major scholarly impact.\n- In \"Rhetoric,\" Aristotle identifies five canons of rhetoric: invention, arrangement, style, memory, and delivery.",
